Nomi <dragonforcemola@gmail.com> wrote:
> I thought of this after playing Crawl for a bit, and realized NetHack
> is somewhat unbalanced, i mean, everyone uses long swords or daggers,
> gets mithril, goes to the castle, and gets some dsm flavor.

I think that's not what usually gets called "unbalanced" but the
problem that "every character looks the same in the end game and has
the same ascension kit".

> Tell me what you think about this:
> These are my ideas to balance some weapons, armour and monsters, will
> post the remaining later.

[Merging skills]
I already thought about doing this for UnNetHack, but I didn't want to
do it before I had an in-game information screen that would tell you
about the skills of weapons.

Even in vanilla there are some surprising gotchas: Javelins and spears
belong to separate skills or katanas and long swords sharing a skill.

> -Merge dagger, knife, short sword and saber skills into Short Blades

I think daggers should be not put into this category. There a lot of
daggers in the dungeons and there main use is throwing them and not
being wielded like the others.

Scimitars should probably also be put into short blades.

> -Merge spear, trident, and polearms into Polearms, make them useful in
> melee without the need to ride
> -Merge dart, shuriken, boomerang and javelin into Throwables

I would merge javelins with spears.

Merging of darts and shurikens is a good idea IMO.

> -Merge mace, club, hammer and morningstar into Maces
> -Merge whip and flail into Flails

Crawl goes as far as having a "Maces & Flails" skill.

> -Merge axes and battleaxes into Axes

Axes and battle-axes already share the same skills.

What about merging pick-axes and axes? In real life a pick-axe is
probably less different from an axe than an one handed axe is from a
two-handed battle-axe.

> -Buff armor: leather (3 ac, 50 weight, mc1), studded leather(4 ac, 60
> weight, mc1), remove ring mail, scale mail (6 ac, 80 weight, mc2),
> remove orcish ring and chain mails, remove banded mail, remove
> mithril, splint mail (8 ac, 130 weight, mc2), plate mail (10 ac, 200
> weight, mc3), bronze plate mail (13 ac, 250 weight, mc3), and crystal
> plate mail (15 ac, 300 weight, reflection, mc3), make the plate mails
> rare (the yendorian army can't be generated with it)
[...]
> -Nerf DSM: (200 weight, 8 ac)

Why buff? In the endgame the player has usually at least AC:-30 which
means he's extremely hard to get hit by monsters.

I'd rather reduce the superior AC of DSMs and maybe even reduce the
maximal safe enchantments of armor and maybe (like Crawl) different
enchantements limits for armor (e.g. lower limites for cloaks and
t-shirts).

> -Knights get +0 studded leather instead of +1 ring mail

I've always thought that even though knights are armored like a tank
from the start, it is balanced by the fact that they also burdened
quite easily because of it.

Of course you can ride but that is not completely trouble free
in the beginning.

> -Be unable to get both cold resistance and fire resistance
> intrinsically

Something like the Fire XOR Cold patch?
http://bilious.alt.org/?171

This only leads to stupid ring or armor switch sessions and is rather
tedious for the player.

> -Give the heart of ahriman flight and invocable displacement

UnNetHack has the Heart of Ahriman giving you faster energy
regeneration like the Eye of the Aethiopica and also permanent
displacement when carried.

> -Remove amnesia
> -Make flayers ignore E a la minotaur

If you removed amnesia, flayers are useless and could be removed
themselves.

No need the keep the one trick pony around if you kill the one trick.

UnNetHack has no scroll of amnesia anymore. So the only sources of
amnesia are the flayers and the new end boss.

I think completely removing it is not really an improvement. A player
reaching the sanctum will most likely only have experienced amnesia by
accident. And if he can fight and kill the end boss in UnNetHack, the
suffered amnesia is only a minor hindrance to ascension.

